 "result": "**Decorator:** `@needs_app_scope` (defined in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`). Apply it under `@click.command(...)`, as `shell_command` and `routes_command` do (`src/tessel/cli.py:998-1060`). It loads the app and pushes the app context for the callback.\n\n- **No decorator needed:** commands registered via `app.cli.command()` or `bundle.cli`. `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`) wraps them automatically, and you can opt out with `needs_app_scope=False`.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (line 333) is what `needs_app_scope` calls via `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo)`. The top-level CLI group is `TesselGroup` (line 531), which subclasses `AppGroup`.",
